{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "843f2266",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# CUAD model selection: tokenizer check and short tests\n",
    "\n",
    "Selected T4 **GPU runtime**, then run the cells in order. This notebook delegates\n",
    "all work to `scripts/model_selection.py`; it compares `bert-base-uncased`,\n",
    "`legal-bert-base-uncased` and `deberta-v3-base`.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Recount** every chunk's length under each candidate tokenizer (special tokens included, no truncation).\n",
    "2. **Short test** each candidate on the *same* subset of fold-0 training contracts, scored on the *full* fold-0 validation split with identical settings.\n",
    "3. **Summarize** results for `docs/model-selection.md`.\n",
    "\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "53dee0ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/Break-Through-Tech/Accenture-1T-contract-review-challenge.git\"\n",
    "REPO_REF = \"task-10-selection\"\n",
    "REPO_DIR = Path(\"/content/contract-review\")\n",
    "\n",
    "CANDIDATES = [\"bert\", \"legal-bert\", \"deberta-v3\"]\n",
    "TRAIN_CONTRACTS = 60   # fold-0 training contracts per run; 0 = all (~326, slow)\n",
    "EPOCHS = 2\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 4         # lower to 2 if deberta-v3 runs out of GPU memory\n",
    "LEARNING_RATE = 2e-5\n",
    "SEEDS = [42]           # add 43, 44 for a steadier comparison (each seed re-runs every candidate)\n",
    "VALIDATION_FOLD = 0\n",
    "RUN_NAME = \"selection-\" + datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y%m%d-%H%M%S\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd1dc7d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Checkout and locked environment\n",
    "An existing checkout is used as-is (no pull). The locked environment does not include the\n",
    "extra packages deberta-v3's tokenizer conversion needs, so they are installed on top of it;\n",
    "`uv add sentencepiece protobuf` in the repo makes this permanent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "95ae5e17",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if not REPO_DIR.exists():\n",
    "    subprocess.run(\n",
    "        [\"git\", \"clone\", \"--branch\", REPO_REF, \"--single-branch\", REPO_URL, str(REPO_DIR)],\n",
    "        check=True,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "required = [\n",
    "    \"pyproject.toml\", \"uv.lock\", \"src/train.py\", \"src/candidates.py\",\n",
    "    \"scripts/model_selection.py\", \"data/train_separate_questions.json\",\n",
    "    \"docs/tuned-baseline-results/folds.csv\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "missing = [name for name in required if not (REPO_DIR / name).is_file()]\n",
    "if missing:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "        f\"Checkout is missing {missing}. Push the implementation or upload a complete checkout.\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"uv\"], check=True)\n",
    "UV = [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"uv\"]\n",
    "subprocess.run(UV + [\"sync\", \"--locked\", \"--dev\", \"--python\", \"3.12\"], cwd=REPO_DIR, check=True)\n",
    "subprocess.run(\n",
    "    UV + [\"pip\", \"install\", \"sentencepiece\", \"protobuf\", \"tiktoken\", \"scikit-learn\"],\n",
    "    cwd=REPO_DIR, check=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_project(*args):\n",
    "    return subprocess.run(\n",
    "        UV + [\"run\", \"--locked\", \"--no-sync\", *map(str, args)], cwd=REPO_DIR, check=True,\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1327e741",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. GPU and software checks\n",
    "Stop here if the CUDA check fails. The tests are offline and fast."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3f034efe",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "run_project(\"python\", \"-c\", '''\n",
    "import torch, transformers\n",
    "print(\"PyTorch:\", torch.__version__, \"CUDA runtime:\", torch.version.cuda)\n",
    "print(\"Transformers:\", transformers.__version__)\n",
    "assert torch.cuda.is_available(), \"No usable CUDA device in the project environment\"\n",
    "print(\"GPU:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0),\n",
    "      f\"{torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 2**30:.1f} GiB\")\n",
    "x = torch.ones(2, device=\"cuda\", requires_grad=True)\n",
    "x.square().sum().backward()\n",
    "torch.cuda.synchronize()\n",
    "assert torch.equal(x.grad.cpu(), torch.tensor([2.0, 2.0]))\n",
    "print(\"GPU tensor and gradient check: PASS\")\n",
    "''')\n",
    "run_project(\"python\", \"-B\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\", \"-p\", \"no:cacheprovider\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "250efe04",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Generate training chunks and labels\n",
    "Same commands as the training notebook. Chunks are the existing 512-token BERT chunks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "69620d3a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "run_project(\"python\", \"-B\", \"-m\", \"scripts.export_chunks\", \"--split\", \"train\")\n",
    "run_project(\"python\", \"-B\", \"-m\", \"scripts.label_chunks\", \"--split\", \"train\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "abd257ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Recount chunk lengths under each tokenizer\n",
    "Downloads the three tokenizers only. `over_limit` is the number of chunks above 512 tokens under\n",
    "that tokenizer; `positives_in_over_limit` shows how much labeled evidence those chunks hold."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8a955e57",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "OUT = REPO_DIR / \"data\" / \"interim\" / \"model-selection\" / RUN_NAME\n",
    "run_project(\"python\", \"-B\", \"-m\", \"scripts.model_selection\", \"count\", \"--output-dir\", OUT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8fc352e0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = pd.read_csv(OUT / \"tokenizer_summary.csv\")\n",
    "display(summary)\n",
    "print(json.dumps(json.loads((OUT / \"tokenizer_meta.json\").read_text()), indent=2))\n",
    "\n",
    "lengths = pd.read_parquet(OUT / \"chunk_lengths.parquet\")\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "for key in CANDIDATES:\n",
    "    ax.hist(lengths[f\"len_{key}\"], bins=60, histtype=\"step\", label=key)\n",
    "ax.axvline(512, color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\", label=\"512 limit\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"tokens per chunk (with special tokens)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"chunks\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(OUT / \"chunk_length_histogram.png\", dpi=150)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "fits_all = (lengths[[f\"len_{k}\" for k in CANDIDATES]].max(axis=1) <= 512)\n",
    "print(f\"Chunks that fit 512 under ALL tokenizers: {fits_all.sum()} of {len(lengths)} \"\n",
    "      f\"({(~fits_all).sum()} will be excluded from the short tests for every candidate)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "68c08a11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Short fine-tuning tests\n",
    "Each run writes `result.json`, `per_category.csv` and validation predictions. A failed candidate\n",
    "(for example GPU out-of-memory) is reported and the loop continues."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a255576b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "failed = []\n",
    "for seed in SEEDS:\n",
    "    for key in CANDIDATES:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n===== {key} seed={seed} =====\", flush=True)\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            run_project(\n",
    "                \"python\", \"-B\", \"-m\", \"scripts.model_selection\", \"train\",\n",
    "                \"--candidate\", key, \"--lengths\", OUT / \"chunk_lengths.parquet\",\n",
    "                \"--output-dir\", OUT / \"runs\", \"--seed\", seed,\n",
    "                \"--train-contracts\", TRAIN_CONTRACTS, \"--epochs\", EPOCHS,\n",
    "                \"--batch-size\", BATCH_SIZE, \"--learning-rate\", LEARNING_RATE,\n",
    "                \"--validation-fold\", VALIDATION_FOLD,\n",
    "            )\n",
    "        except subprocess.CalledProcessError as exc:\n",
    "            failed.append((key, seed))\n",
    "            print(f\"FAILED: {key} seed={seed} ({exc}). See the traceback above.\")\n",
    "print(\"Failed runs:\", failed or \"none\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44717408",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Compare and download\n",
    "Rank mainly on **macro average precision** (threshold-free, so it still separates models when\n",
    "a short run has not yet learned to cross 0.5). F1 at 0.5 will be near zero for rare categories after a\n",
    "small budget; the best-threshold F1 is tuned on the validation fold itself, so treat it as optimistic."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4ca60428",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = pd.DataFrame([json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in sorted((OUT / \"runs\").glob(\"*/result.json\"))])\n",
    "cols = [\"candidate\", \"seed\", \"macro_average_precision\", \"macro_f1_best_threshold_on_validation\",\n",
    "        \"macro_f1_at_0.5\", \"micro_f1_at_0.5\", \"validation_loss\", \"categories_with_positives\",\n",
    "        \"seconds_per_step\", \"train_seconds\", \"peak_gpu_gib\", \"parameters_millions\"]\n",
    "display(results[cols])\n",
    "if len(SEEDS) > 1:\n",
    "    display(results.groupby(\"candidate\")[cols[2:]].agg([\"mean\", \"std\"]).round(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "per_category = pd.concat(\n",
    "    {p.parent.name: pd.read_csv(p).set_index(\"category\")[\"average_precision\"]\n",
    "     for p in sorted((OUT / \"runs\").glob(\"*/per_category.csv\"))}, axis=1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(per_category.round(3))\n",
    "results.to_csv(OUT / \"results_summary.csv\", index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8cbf085e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import shutil\n",
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "\n",
    "archive = shutil.make_archive(\n",
    "    str(REPO_DIR.parent / RUN_NAME), \"zip\", root_dir=OUT.parent, base_dir=OUT.name,\n",
    ")\n",
    "files.download(archive)"
   ]
  }
 ],
